    qa_wh_test.go:28: found=true row=map[email:jane@example.com id:7 updated_at:2026-10-22 10:00:00]
    qa_wh_test.go:29: SQL sent: SELECT * FROM `analytics`.`customers` FINAL WHERE `email` = ? LIMIT 1 args=[jane@example.com]
--- FAIL: TestQA_RowByAnyColumnWithoutPrimaryKeyColumn (0.00s)
    qa_wh_test.go:26: err=<nil> summary="found: yes, updated_at=2026-10-11T10:00:00Z" rowCalls=1
    qa_wh_test.go:28: warehouse_row by a non-key column was answered on a clickhouse warehouse
--- FAIL: TestQA_WarehouseRowByEmailOnClickHouse (0.00s)
```

**Suggested fix:** Add `(*Client).PrimaryKeyColumn` reading `system.tables.primary_key` (or `sorting_key`) for the db/table with bound parameters, returning `clients.ErrNotFound` when empty and `clients.ErrNotSupported` when it has more than one column, as the Snowflake and Databricks clients do. Alternatively make `warehouse_row` and `checkSinkKey` fail closed when the warehouse lacks the method. Add the clickhouse case to `wh_row_key_test.go` with a fake that has no `PrimaryKeyColumn`.
